WEBVTT

00:00:01.140 --> 00:00:03.220
The second round of the finals of the Monaco Cup.

00:00:03.220 --> 00:00:07.480
The clash of Kawachi’s Victory and Shachihoko´s Alexandria.

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:09.400
It’s done!

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:12.900
This is my masterpiece, made with kodaimai-miso!

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:14.870
Alexandria!

00:00:16.030 --> 00:00:17.820
Oh! What did you just say?!

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:20.320
Your name was Conan, right?

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:21.410
I’m talking about you.

00:00:21.410 --> 00:00:23.330
I’m saying that Conan was singing his own praises.

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:24.750
Huh?

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:26.040
Conan was singing his own praises...

00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:26.870
Conan temaemiso.

00:00:26.870 --> 00:00:28.420
Conan temaemiso! Conan temaemiso!

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:29.880
Co...

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:33.800
Kodaimai-miso!

00:00:34.250 --> 00:00:38.680
And, Pierrot risked his life on this high-level offense and defense.

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:43.220
This is my revolutionary dinner bread.

00:00:43.220 --> 00:00:44.980
This is Victory!

00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:47.770
Well then, let’s dig in mambo.

00:00:48.980 --> 00:00:51.520
It isn’t just some stupid story.

00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:53.530
It’s the story of Libya and me.

00:00:55.650 --> 00:00:57.550
The story of Libya and me.

00:00:58.610 --> 00:01:01.040
Libya and me.

00:01:01.910 --> 00:01:03.540
Libya and me?

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:06.590
Libya and me.

00:01:07.290 --> 00:01:09.300
Boku to Libya.

00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:13.550
It’s Victory!

00:01:14.130 --> 00:01:16.340
Congratulations, Kawachi.

00:01:16.340 --> 00:01:18.010
You’ve won.

00:01:18.010 --> 00:01:19.560
It’s your victory.

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:23.930
Despite injuries, the results of the match were released, and Kawachi won.

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:25.890
Pierrot!

00:01:25.890 --> 00:01:28.600
I-It was delicious.

00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:33.360
The bread of your father’s dreams.

00:01:35.150 --> 00:01:40.910
I... I also... want to meet... my father...

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:46.630
But, Pierrot was carried to the hospital.

00:01:48.540 --> 00:01:50.040
Father!

00:01:56.120 --> 00:01:58.450
There’s English bread, German bread, and French bread,

00:01:58.450 --> 00:02:00.270
but Japan’s bread, <i>Japan</i>, does not exist.

00:02:00.270 --> 00:02:02.650
In that case, there’s no choice but to create it.

00:02:02.650 --> 00:02:05.970
This story is a serious, biographical ballad of a boy who possesses Solar Hands,

00:02:05.970 --> 00:02:11.200
Azuma Kazuma, who will create a Japanese bread made by and for the Japanese people,

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:15.310
which can be presented to the world proudly.

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:49.080
Reunion at the VIP seat!!

00:03:49.080 --> 00:03:50.460
Heaven again!

00:03:52.450 --> 00:03:53.410
No!

00:03:53.410 --> 00:03:54.500
Please stop that!

00:03:56.710 --> 00:03:58.970
It’s all right.

00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:02.890
Please stop that.

00:04:04.970 --> 00:04:05.840
Pierrot-san.

00:04:05.840 --> 00:04:06.800
Vitals falling.

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:07.510
Heart and pulse rates dropping.

00:04:07.510 --> 00:04:08.340
Pierrot-san!
Heart and pulse rates dropping.

00:04:08.340 --> 00:04:09.300
We’re losing him!

00:04:09.300 --> 00:04:10.980
Hang in there, Pierrot-san!

00:04:15.980 --> 00:04:16.990
Pierrot...

00:04:17.850 --> 00:04:18.980
This is an emergency broadcast.

00:04:19.480 --> 00:04:21.820
We just received information from the Monaco Royal Hospital that

00:04:21.820 --> 00:04:24.600
Mr. Pierrot, who is presently in critical condition,

00:04:24.600 --> 00:04:26.400
has been confirmed to have the Bombay blood type,

00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:28.410
which only a few hundred people in the world have.

00:04:28.410 --> 00:04:30.040
C-Critical condition?

00:04:30.580 --> 00:04:35.710
If there is someone here with the same blood type, Bombay blood, please step forward.

00:04:35.710 --> 00:04:37.040
Bombay blood?

00:04:37.670 --> 00:04:38.540
It... It can’t be!

00:04:40.040 --> 00:04:42.300
What is the Bombay blood type?

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:47.630
In addition to the commonly known blood types of A, B, AB and O,

00:04:47.630 --> 00:04:49.310
there are many other different blood types.

00:04:50.180 --> 00:04:51.870
Even amongst those,

00:04:51.870 --> 00:04:56.060
Bombay blood is a very rare blood type, found in only 1 in 10 million people.

00:04:56.060 --> 00:04:59.400
It has a characteristic that makes it very different from other blood types.

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:00.270
What?

00:05:00.270 --> 00:05:01.530
What’s so different about it?

00:05:01.810 --> 00:05:06.280
People with Bombay blood can’t receive transfusions from any other blood types.

00:05:07.780 --> 00:05:11.160
So, if there isn’t anybody here with Bombay blood,

00:05:11.160 --> 00:05:13.030
Pierrot-san will...

00:05:13.030 --> 00:05:14.290
It... It can’t be...

00:05:18.670 --> 00:05:19.500
I’ll look for it!

00:05:21.710 --> 00:05:22.510
It’s impossible.

00:05:22.510 --> 00:05:26.270
If there’s only a few hundred people in the world with this blood type,

00:05:26.270 --> 00:05:27.560
we couldn’t possibly...

00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:30.010
You’re going to give up, Kawachi?!

00:05:30.800 --> 00:05:32.260
Th-That’s right.

00:05:32.260 --> 00:05:34.270
I have a tendency to give up when things go bad.

00:05:34.640 --> 00:05:37.600
I won’t give up as easily anymore.

00:05:37.600 --> 00:05:41.530
It was only after promising myself this that I was able to create Victory.

00:05:42.020 --> 00:05:43.400
Tsukino! Kanmuri!

00:05:43.400 --> 00:05:45.280
The two of you, try searching in the tournament hall.

00:05:46.780 --> 00:05:47.890
Very well.

00:05:47.890 --> 00:05:48.780
It would be my pleasure.

00:05:49.240 --> 00:05:50.320
Azuma!

00:05:50.320 --> 00:05:52.870
You and I will go around Monaco in search of it!

00:05:52.870 --> 00:05:53.950
A-All right!

00:05:53.950 --> 00:05:55.790
We’ll help, too.

00:05:56.330 --> 00:05:57.500
Manager...

00:05:57.500 --> 00:05:58.500
Me, too!

00:05:58.500 --> 00:05:59.540
Shachihoko!

00:06:00.160 --> 00:06:01.500
Ryou, we should go, too.

00:06:01.500 --> 00:06:03.710
Yeah, we should.

00:06:03.710 --> 00:06:05.340
All right! Me, too!

00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:06.470
I’ll come, too.

00:06:06.840 --> 00:06:08.220
Everyone...

00:06:08.800 --> 00:06:10.550
All right!

00:06:10.550 --> 00:06:13.550
No matter what, we’ll definitely find us some Bombay blood–

00:06:13.550 --> 00:06:15.520
That is not necessary.

00:06:18.480 --> 00:06:19.770
Your Majesty.

00:06:19.770 --> 00:06:21.730
What do you mean, it’s not necessary?!

00:06:22.270 --> 00:06:24.950
If you need someone with Bombay blood,

00:06:25.300 --> 00:06:26.200
then he is right here!

00:06:27.230 --> 00:06:28.900
Get the car ready!

00:06:28.900 --> 00:06:29.450
Yes, sir!

00:06:31.910 --> 00:06:33.620
Is that for real?

00:06:33.620 --> 00:06:35.960
The King of Monaco has Bombay blood?

00:06:37.330 --> 00:06:39.250
What’s eating you, Ryou?

00:06:39.250 --> 00:06:44.710
You can’t be born with Bombay blood unless both your parents carry the same gene.

00:06:44.710 --> 00:06:48.380
They’re usually born in places with a custom of close relatives marrying each other.

00:06:49.170 --> 00:06:54.100
In most countries, royalty tend
to marry close relatives, right?

00:06:55.140 --> 00:06:56.140
Wait a minute.

00:06:56.140 --> 00:06:57.390
Then, Pierrot is...?

00:06:57.740 --> 00:06:58.390
Yeah.

00:06:58.390 --> 00:07:01.860
The King of Monaco and Pierrot may be blood relatives.

00:07:02.190 --> 00:07:03.480
Eh?!

00:07:03.480 --> 00:07:06.270
Monaco Royal Hospital

00:07:06.270 --> 00:07:06.650
Hey! Do we still not have the blood?!
Monaco Royal Hospital

00:07:06.650 --> 00:07:07.570
Hey! Do we still not have the blood?!

00:07:07.570 --> 00:07:09.360
It’s supposed to be coming within the next five minutes.

00:07:09.360 --> 00:07:10.150
Pulse?

00:07:10.150 --> 00:07:11.950
He’s in a pretty critical state.

00:07:11.950 --> 00:07:14.960
In the end... You never came for me.

00:07:15.620 --> 00:07:17.920
Father... Mother...

00:07:18.380 --> 00:07:22.460
You abandoned me in the tent of the Quedam Circus.

00:07:23.580 --> 00:07:28.700
I believed that if I simply
became famous, you’d come to get me.

00:07:29.310 --> 00:07:34.800
So, I worked hard... and worked some
more... and became a world-level clown.

00:07:34.800 --> 00:07:37.850
But, it was all in vain.

00:07:38.720 --> 00:07:42.850
You never planned on looking
for me from the very beginning.

00:07:42.850 --> 00:07:47.950
You’re so cruel... Father... Mother...

00:07:57.070 --> 00:07:59.580
Th... This is...?

00:07:59.990 --> 00:08:01.080
Welcome!

00:08:01.700 --> 00:08:03.960
Welcome to Cabaret Club Heaven!

00:08:04.460 --> 00:08:07.460
One table, coming right up!

00:08:09.380 --> 00:08:10.300
No way!

00:08:10.300 --> 00:08:12.460
You lost your life over the judging of a bread...?

00:08:12.460 --> 00:08:13.170
Yeah.

00:08:13.170 --> 00:08:14.420
I’m a clown, after all...

00:08:14.420 --> 00:08:16.550
But, I must seem really stupid, right?

00:08:16.550 --> 00:08:18.230
That’s not true!

00:08:18.850 --> 00:08:20.050
Because...

00:08:20.050 --> 00:08:25.980
The man I loved before was an idiot
who came here while judging bread, too.

00:08:25.980 --> 00:08:27.570
What are you talking about?

00:08:27.980 --> 00:08:29.400
Sorry for the wait.

00:08:30.650 --> 00:08:32.280
I didn’t order this.

00:08:33.030 --> 00:08:35.240
The customer over there sent it over.

00:08:36.650 --> 00:08:38.240
Yo, Pierrot-kun.

00:08:38.660 --> 00:08:39.820
Your Majesty!

00:08:39.820 --> 00:08:41.250
Why are you here?

00:08:41.660 --> 00:08:43.450
Well, it doesn’t really matter, does it?

00:08:43.450 --> 00:08:46.250
More importantly, wouldn’t you like to sit next to me?

00:08:52.800 --> 00:08:54.590
By the way, Pierrot-kun...

00:08:54.590 --> 00:08:58.260
From what I hear, you were abandoned by your parents?

00:08:58.260 --> 00:09:00.720
How many years ago did this happen?

00:09:00.720 --> 00:09:03.890
Umm... Well, I’m almost 23, so...

00:09:03.890 --> 00:09:06.270
It happened about 23 years ago.

00:09:06.890 --> 00:09:08.560
23 years ago?!

00:09:09.400 --> 00:09:11.110
23 years ago...

00:09:11.110 --> 00:09:13.570
And he has Bombay blood, like me...

00:09:13.570 --> 00:09:14.780
There’s no mistake about it.

00:09:15.280 --> 00:09:18.620
Why didn’t I notice until now?

00:09:19.990 --> 00:09:21.160
Your Majesty...

00:09:21.870 --> 00:09:23.000
Your Majesty!

00:09:23.410 --> 00:09:25.250
Is something the matter?

00:09:28.330 --> 00:09:30.960
J-Just talking possibilities here...

00:09:30.960 --> 00:09:34.090
But, what would you do if your
parents were next to you right now?

00:09:34.090 --> 00:09:35.220
Eh?

00:09:36.630 --> 00:09:39.050
I can hug him right away.

00:09:39.050 --> 00:09:40.510
Because I am...

00:09:40.990 --> 00:09:42.600
I don’t really care anymore.

00:09:42.600 --> 00:09:45.730
I no longer want to meet
people like that, even one tiny bit.

00:09:47.850 --> 00:09:49.480
I mean, don’t you think so, too?

00:09:49.480 --> 00:09:51.980
Right now, I’m the most famous clown in the world.

00:09:52.480 --> 00:09:57.110
If they regretted abandoning me even a little,
they would’ve found me a long time ago.

00:09:57.700 --> 00:09:59.620
Don’t you think so as well, Your Majesty?

00:09:59.620 --> 00:10:01.070
That’s not true.

00:10:01.070 --> 00:10:01.910
Huh?

00:10:01.910 --> 00:10:03.910
Uh... no.

00:10:03.910 --> 00:10:07.410
Your parents may have had circumstances that prevented them...

00:10:07.410 --> 00:10:09.500
Circumstances?!

00:10:09.500 --> 00:10:11.630
If they did, then I’d really like an explanation of it.

00:10:12.370 --> 00:10:13.200
Well...

00:10:14.420 --> 00:10:17.510
Well, I don’t really think there are any circumstances

00:10:17.510 --> 00:10:19.760
that an abandoned child could comprehend.

00:10:19.760 --> 00:10:21.470
It was a mistake.

00:10:21.840 --> 00:10:22.300
Huh?

00:10:24.180 --> 00:10:29.180
It may be that something unfortunate
happened outside of your parents’ control.

00:10:29.180 --> 00:10:31.560
You’re acting strange, Your Majesty.

00:10:31.560 --> 00:10:34.650
You’re speaking almost as
though you know my parents.

00:10:35.520 --> 00:10:37.780
Well, I am your...

00:10:37.780 --> 00:10:38.990
Oh, I see.

00:10:40.570 --> 00:10:42.240
It’s all right, Your Majesty.

00:10:42.240 --> 00:10:44.410
You’re trying to comfort me, right?

00:10:44.410 --> 00:10:45.700
No, that’s not it.

00:10:45.700 --> 00:10:47.580
Please don’t worry.

00:10:47.580 --> 00:10:53.760
I no longer want people who’ve abandoned their child to come for me anymore.

00:11:01.380 --> 00:11:02.720
I wonder if he’s all right...?

00:11:02.720 --> 00:11:06.470
It’s been quite a while since the operation began.

00:11:07.100 --> 00:11:08.140
We have trouble!

00:11:08.140 --> 00:11:09.060
What’s wrong?

00:11:09.060 --> 00:11:11.520
His Majesty is ignoring the doctor’s advice,

00:11:11.520 --> 00:11:13.550
and has ordered for an unreasonable
amount of blood to be transfused.

00:11:14.480 --> 00:11:17.490
Now, even the king is in critical condition!

00:11:28.700 --> 00:11:30.750
It looks like we can now be certain about it.

00:11:30.750 --> 00:11:33.460
You mean that the king’s father is Pierrot, right?

00:11:34.330 --> 00:11:35.540
No, it’s the other way around!

00:11:36.330 --> 00:11:39.300
But, isn’t it too early to come to that conclusion?

00:11:40.170 --> 00:11:43.680
Where would you find someone noble enough to be willing to donate so much blood,

00:11:43.680 --> 00:11:45.800
risking his own life for a complete stranger?

00:11:45.800 --> 00:11:49.810
I think we can conclude that the same thing came into the king’s mind.

00:11:50.560 --> 00:11:52.230
As expected of you, Kuroyanagi-san.

00:11:52.230 --> 00:11:53.270
Brilliant deductive work.

00:11:54.190 --> 00:11:55.020
It’s the old man!

00:11:55.020 --> 00:11:56.190
Pharaoh!

00:11:56.190 --> 00:11:57.270
Why are you here?

00:11:57.270 --> 00:11:59.820
We’re the Monaco Secret Police.

00:11:59.820 --> 00:12:03.280
If something were to happen to the king,
we would be informed immediately.

00:12:03.280 --> 00:12:05.990
So... Why do you say that it’s brilliant deductive work?

00:12:05.990 --> 00:12:11.660
As Kuroyanagi-san deduced,
the King of Monaco has a son.

00:12:11.660 --> 00:12:13.620
I believe I’ve already
mentioned this to you.

00:12:13.620 --> 00:12:17.170
The Monaco Royal Family has an unusual tradition.

00:12:17.170 --> 00:12:19.040
According to the
Royal Family Code, Article XIV:

00:12:19.040 --> 00:12:24.170
“As the lion does with its cub, the Child must be dropped into a valley 1000 fathoms...”

00:12:24.170 --> 00:12:25.880
W-Wait a moment.

00:12:25.880 --> 00:12:27.800
Your stories usually tend to be long.

00:12:27.800 --> 00:12:29.850
So, get to the point, will you?

00:12:29.850 --> 00:12:31.220
Very well.

00:12:31.220 --> 00:12:32.560
In other words...

00:12:33.180 --> 00:12:36.600
In order for children of the Royal Family
to learn of the hardships of the citizens,

00:12:36.600 --> 00:12:41.550
they are raised within a
common middle-class household.

00:12:41.550 --> 00:12:44.160
But... 23 years ago...

00:12:44.690 --> 00:12:46.160
You want to end the practice?!

00:12:46.160 --> 00:12:47.280
Yes.

00:12:47.280 --> 00:12:48.410
I have decided.

00:12:48.410 --> 00:12:49.820
What are you saying?!

00:12:49.820 --> 00:12:52.950
You cannot change a tradition that has continued for so many hundreds of years so easily.

00:12:52.950 --> 00:12:56.250
It’s certain that other Royal
Family members will protest.

00:12:56.860 --> 00:12:58.040
I am sure they will.

00:12:58.040 --> 00:12:59.170
In that case...

00:12:59.630 --> 00:13:02.690
From this day forth, I no longer have a child!

00:13:02.690 --> 00:13:05.670
My newborn son, Prince Leol.

00:13:05.670 --> 00:13:08.260
I will have him raised with a regular family immediately.

00:13:08.260 --> 00:13:10.770
W-What are you saying?!

00:13:11.180 --> 00:13:12.770
Listen, Pharaoh.

00:13:13.430 --> 00:13:17.780
In accordance with the tradition,
I was sent to a baker’s home at age eight.

00:13:18.690 --> 00:13:20.560
It was lonely and sad.

00:13:20.560 --> 00:13:22.520
I cried every day.

00:13:23.690 --> 00:13:28.240
A child brought up as the prince is
suddenly separated from his parents,

00:13:28.240 --> 00:13:30.620
and lives as the child of a common citizen.

00:13:31.370 --> 00:13:34.350
That change in environment is nothing but terrifying,

00:13:34.350 --> 00:13:37.170
and merely leads to the warping of one’s personality.

00:13:37.660 --> 00:13:39.630
B-But...

00:13:40.000 --> 00:13:43.420
Back then, the only reason I
was able to conquer that fate was

00:13:43.420 --> 00:13:47.310
because of a chance meeting with a baker, Kirisaki.

00:13:49.180 --> 00:13:50.590
In other words...

00:13:50.590 --> 00:13:53.510
We might as well raise him as a
child of the masses from the very start.

00:13:53.510 --> 00:13:58.730
I believe that learning that he is a
Prince later in life would then save this child.

00:13:59.190 --> 00:14:00.730
Your Majesty...

00:14:01.400 --> 00:14:02.560
And so...

00:14:02.560 --> 00:14:08.410
The newborn Prince Leol was given into
the care of the chosen middle-class family.

00:14:08.780 --> 00:14:09.740
But...

00:14:09.740 --> 00:14:11.740
W-We have trouble!

00:14:11.740 --> 00:14:16.080
That family has taken the money given
to them and disappeared with the prince!

00:14:20.750 --> 00:14:24.880
At that time, thanks to our
investigation, we discovered the couple,

00:14:24.880 --> 00:14:29.260
and we found that they committed suicide
outside the country after their escape failed.

00:14:29.260 --> 00:14:31.840
But Prince Leol was nowhere to be found.

00:14:31.840 --> 00:14:36.770
We thought that Prince Leol had
been murdered during their escape.

00:14:36.770 --> 00:14:38.350
Then...

00:14:38.350 --> 00:14:42.280
Based on his age and his blood type,
we believe that there is no mistake about it.

00:14:42.770 --> 00:14:45.060
Pierrot-sama is Prince Leol...

00:14:45.060 --> 00:14:48.780
The person to become the
next King of Monaco, Leonhart XV!

00:14:52.280 --> 00:14:53.320
I see.

00:14:53.320 --> 00:14:56.410
Pierrot-san has had a really hard life.

00:14:56.410 --> 00:14:58.200
Exactly! Right? Right?

00:14:58.200 --> 00:15:00.290
No! Stop that!

00:15:00.290 --> 00:15:05.210
Really. That damn old man and old hag...

00:15:05.210 --> 00:15:07.460
I won’t forgive them, no matter what!

00:15:07.460 --> 00:15:11.550
If they have the cheek to show up,
I’ll multiply and beat ’em up.

00:15:11.550 --> 00:15:12.470
I am sorry.

00:15:13.470 --> 00:15:16.680
Why are you apologizing so much, Your Majesty?

00:15:16.680 --> 00:15:18.180
We’re dead now, aren’t we?

00:15:18.180 --> 00:15:20.270
So, let’s just drink up.

00:15:21.640 --> 00:15:24.480
Come to think of it, why did you die?

00:15:24.480 --> 00:15:25.900
I will not let you die.

00:15:26.480 --> 00:15:27.400
I will not...

00:15:28.100 --> 00:15:28.900
I will not...

00:15:29.690 --> 00:15:32.410
I absolutely will not allow you to die!

00:15:32.940 --> 00:15:33.910
Leol!

00:15:33.910 --> 00:15:35.160
You must live!

00:15:35.530 --> 00:15:37.870
Huh? L-Leol?

00:15:37.870 --> 00:15:39.290
That is correct.

00:15:39.290 --> 00:15:41.080
Your name is Leol.

00:15:41.080 --> 00:15:43.290
You were born as the Prince of Monaco.

00:15:43.290 --> 00:15:45.880
You are the man to become Leonhart XV.

00:15:45.880 --> 00:15:46.380
And...

00:15:47.000 --> 00:15:48.380
You are my son!

00:15:49.090 --> 00:15:50.630
Note: “Pokaan” is the sound effect you hear in the background.
Pokaan

00:15:50.630 --> 00:15:52.100
Note: “Pokaan” is the sound effect you hear in the background.

00:15:52.340 --> 00:15:53.470
Doctor, it’s no use!

00:15:53.470 --> 00:15:55.300
The king is holding it with amazing strength!

00:15:55.300 --> 00:15:57.350
We can’t get the transfusion needle out!

00:15:57.930 --> 00:15:58.720
The fool!

00:15:58.720 --> 00:16:01.390
If humans lose more than half their blood, they die!

00:16:01.390 --> 00:16:03.350
Stop the blood pump!

00:16:03.350 --> 00:16:04.270
Well...

00:16:04.270 --> 00:16:06.100
The break-off switch is broken.

00:16:06.100 --> 00:16:07.360
We can’t turn off the pump!

00:16:08.110 --> 00:16:09.360
How can this be?!

00:16:10.230 --> 00:16:16.320
You’re telling me that the king’s wish
to save this young man is that strong?

00:16:16.950 --> 00:16:18.330
Um... Excuse me...

00:16:18.830 --> 00:16:22.000
Even kings joke around, huh?

00:16:22.000 --> 00:16:23.370
I just sobered up.

00:16:23.370 --> 00:16:25.160
I am not joking!

00:16:25.160 --> 00:16:27.580
No! It has to be a joke!

00:16:27.580 --> 00:16:30.380
You can’t make such horrible jokes just because you’re dead, Your Majesty!

00:16:32.590 --> 00:16:34.890
Kings do not joke.

00:16:37.550 --> 00:16:39.050
Leol...

00:16:39.050 --> 00:16:43.020
Right now, my blood is flowing into your body.

00:16:43.020 --> 00:16:47.350
This blood is Bombay blood, only found
among a few hundred people in the world.

00:16:47.350 --> 00:16:52.400
And, people with Bombay blood cannot
receive anything other than Bombay blood.

00:16:53.190 --> 00:16:58.360
My blood type is Bombay blood...
The same as Your Majesty’s?

00:16:58.360 --> 00:16:59.820
T-Then...

00:16:59.820 --> 00:17:04.250
Could it be that the reason you’re here
is that you’re transfusing blood to me?

00:17:04.870 --> 00:17:08.500
This person is... my father?!

00:17:08.500 --> 00:17:10.750
No way! It can’t be!

00:17:11.310 --> 00:17:14.760
Right now... This person holding me tightly...

00:17:16.510 --> 00:17:21.510
He’s holding me so tight that I can hear his heartbeat.

00:17:21.510 --> 00:17:23.150
This person is...

00:17:25.220 --> 00:17:27.270
His heartbeat is growing weak.

00:17:27.820 --> 00:17:29.240
Your Majesty!

00:17:32.100 --> 00:17:33.440
I am sorry.

00:17:33.440 --> 00:17:35.740
It seems that the time for us to part has come.

00:17:35.740 --> 00:17:36.490
Huh?

00:17:36.490 --> 00:17:37.860
P-Part?

00:17:37.860 --> 00:17:40.160
What lies ahead of death?

00:17:40.160 --> 00:17:43.880
This is where your living or dying is decided.

00:17:43.880 --> 00:17:46.750
In other words, it’s the entrance way to the other world.

00:17:46.750 --> 00:17:48.120
A place for those on the verge of death to socialize.

00:17:48.120 --> 00:17:49.080
Cabaret Club Heaven.

00:17:49.080 --> 00:17:49.840
Huh?

00:17:50.790 --> 00:17:53.420
It seems that you will not die.

00:17:53.420 --> 00:17:55.130
But, His Majesty will die.

00:17:55.130 --> 00:17:56.840
Th-That can’t be!

00:17:56.840 --> 00:17:58.300
I am happy.

00:17:58.300 --> 00:17:58.800
Huh?

00:17:59.590 --> 00:18:04.390
My blood protected you... My son.

00:18:05.220 --> 00:18:10.190
In the very end... I was able to do something fatherly.

00:18:13.650 --> 00:18:15.920
Goodbye, Pierrot-san.

00:18:17.360 --> 00:18:18.320
Wait!

00:18:18.320 --> 00:18:19.660
We still haven’t...

00:18:20.660 --> 00:18:22.210
I can’t move my legs!

00:18:22.780 --> 00:18:24.080
I’m disappearing!

00:18:24.080 --> 00:18:25.500
My body is...

00:18:27.250 --> 00:18:29.000
My voice won’t come out anymore.

00:18:29.000 --> 00:18:30.460
Your Majesty!

00:18:30.460 --> 00:18:31.750
No! Your Majesty!

00:18:31.750 --> 00:18:33.960
Wait!

00:18:33.960 --> 00:18:35.510
I still...

00:18:35.510 --> 00:18:39.010
I finally... I finally met you!

00:18:39.010 --> 00:18:41.510
I’ve been waiting for this moment for...

00:18:42.390 --> 00:18:47.180
If you become that great of a performer, I’m
sure that your parents will come to get you.

00:18:47.180 --> 00:18:48.140
Really?

00:18:48.140 --> 00:18:50.320
I’ve been dreaming of this moment...

00:18:52.810 --> 00:18:56.360
I’ve worked hard for such
long time, for this very day...

00:19:00.700 --> 00:19:06.540
There’s so many... so many things I want to tell you!

00:19:08.330 --> 00:19:11.040
I absolutely don’t want this!

00:19:11.710 --> 00:19:13.250
Wait!

00:19:13.250 --> 00:19:15.050
Please wait!

00:19:15.630 --> 00:19:16.550
Wait!

00:19:20.750 --> 00:19:25.270
Fa... ther...

00:19:33.440 --> 00:19:38.240
L-Leol!

00:19:40.740 --> 00:19:44.740
The King of Monaco... is dead.

00:20:06.270 --> 00:20:09.140
I bet that Pierrot’s depressed.

00:20:09.650 --> 00:20:12.230
We’ve come here to cheer him up,

00:20:12.230 --> 00:20:14.770
but I don’t really know what to say to him.

00:20:15.740 --> 00:20:18.950
If he’s hung up over the past and sulking around,

00:20:18.950 --> 00:20:20.490
then I’ll beat him into shape.

00:20:21.160 --> 00:20:23.740
I hear voices from that room.

00:20:29.210 --> 00:20:31.470
What is this uproar?!

00:20:34.830 --> 00:20:36.710
Oh, look who’s here.

00:20:37.010 --> 00:20:39.180
It’s the Japanese representatives.

00:20:39.180 --> 00:20:40.970
Thank you for coming!

00:20:41.340 --> 00:20:43.720
I’ve been suddenly promoted big time!

00:20:43.720 --> 00:20:47.980
I’m Pierrot, ringmaster of Quedam,
and a king with a criminal record.

00:20:47.980 --> 00:20:50.980
So, come celebrate with us!

00:20:51.400 --> 00:20:52.480
Pierrot...

00:20:52.480 --> 00:20:54.690
It’s so painful that I can’t watch.

00:20:55.860 --> 00:20:58.360
Pierrot, stop with the fake show of courage.

00:21:02.450 --> 00:21:03.620
Your Majesty!

00:21:03.620 --> 00:21:05.200
Come this way, quickly.

00:21:05.200 --> 00:21:06.900
Let’s drink together.

00:21:07.540 --> 00:21:08.620
Party over.

00:21:08.620 --> 00:21:10.000
Huh?

00:21:14.920 --> 00:21:17.540
You probably won’t believe me, but...

00:21:18.800 --> 00:21:20.050
I...

00:21:20.050 --> 00:21:22.550
spoke to my father in heaven.

00:21:24.180 --> 00:21:27.430
At first, I didn’t know that he was my father,

00:21:27.430 --> 00:21:30.150
and I castigated him.

00:21:31.020 --> 00:21:35.950
I didn’t even know that he
was risking his life to save me.

00:21:36.820 --> 00:21:37.690
However...

00:21:37.690 --> 00:21:40.070
I tried to apologize.

00:21:40.070 --> 00:21:43.620
But by then my body had begun to disappear.

00:21:47.790 --> 00:21:51.290
That may be, but nothing will come
of your drowning yourself in alcohol.

00:21:51.290 --> 00:21:53.120
I know that!

00:21:53.120 --> 00:21:56.670
I know that, but... I...

00:21:56.670 --> 00:22:00.800
I can no longer meet Father!

00:22:01.260 --> 00:22:03.000
It’s not like you can no longer meet him.

00:22:03.000 --> 00:22:04.090
Huh?

00:22:04.090 --> 00:22:05.510
I’ll help you meet him.

00:22:05.510 --> 00:22:06.260
Huh?

00:22:06.760 --> 00:22:11.770
In the past, Old Man Kuroyanagi has
gone to heaven after eating my bread.

00:22:11.770 --> 00:22:12.980
Oh yeah!

00:22:12.980 --> 00:22:18.110
<i>Japan</i> #44 might be able to
take Pierrot to heaven once again!

00:22:18.110 --> 00:22:19.780
No, that’s impossible.

00:22:19.780 --> 00:22:20.320
Huh?

00:22:20.320 --> 00:22:23.400
Well, I don’t have the petalite I need to make #44.

00:22:23.400 --> 00:22:25.240
Then, what’ll you do?

00:22:25.240 --> 00:22:26.690
That’s easy.

00:22:26.990 --> 00:22:30.560
All I have to do is make an even more amazing bread!

00:24:05.690 --> 00:24:08.440
Oh, no! Father died!

00:24:08.440 --> 00:24:09.850
I’ll help you meet him.

00:24:09.850 --> 00:24:10.450
Huh?

00:24:10.450 --> 00:24:13.360
By making an amazing bread, I’ll
be sure to help you guys meet again.

00:24:13.360 --> 00:24:15.020
Oh! You sound like the lead actor!

00:24:15.020 --> 00:24:16.350
Next time, on Yakitate!! Japan,

00:24:16.350 --> 00:24:17.490
I’ll show you the universe!!

00:24:17.490 --> 00:24:19.000
The man who’ll inherit the <i>Gopan</i>!

00:24:19.000 --> 00:24:19.900
Be sure to watch.

00:24:20.470 --> 00:24:22.650
Yakitate Seeds of Knowledge!!

00:24:23.010 --> 00:24:26.640
Blood types are classified under the categories of A, O, B, and AB.

00:24:26.640 --> 00:24:28.820
My father and I have Bombay Blood.

00:24:28.820 --> 00:24:31.670
It's an extremely unusual blood type,
labeled as a "Rare Blood."

00:24:32.150 --> 00:24:34.260
EHHHH!?!
